</nav>
<header class="legal-hero kit-reveal">
<p class="kicker legal-eyebrow">
<span class="sr-only">YAP Arena · Legal</span>
<span class="ins" aria-hidden="true">yap arena · legal</span>
</p>
<h1 class="page-title legal-title">
<span class="sr-only">Terms of use</span>
<span class="ins" aria-hidden="true">terms of vse</span>
</h1>
<p class="legal-lede">These terms are the agreement between you and <mark class="legal-todo">[Legal name of the business]</mark> for using YAP Arena. Please read them together with the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
<dl class="legal-meta">
<div>
<dt>Updated</dt>
<dd>
<time datetime="2026-10-30">October 30, 2026</time>
</dd>
</div>
<div>
<dt>Version</dt>
<dd>2026-10-30</dd>
</div>
</dl>
<ul class="legal-glance">
<li>
<strong>18 and older</strong>
<span>You must be at least 18 to create an account or use YAP Arena.</span>
</li>
<li>
<strong>Debates are public</strong>
<span>Debates are recorded and replayed publicly, with captions and an AI outline.</span>
</li>
<li>
<strong>Yap Coins are play money</strong>
<span>They have no cash value and can’t be bought, sold or withdrawn.</span>
</li>
<li>
<strong>Argue the idea</strong>
<span>No harassment, hate, threats, spam or sharing other people’s private information.</span>
</li>
</ul>
</header>
<div class="legal-layout">
<nav class="legal-toc" aria-labelledby="legal-toc-title">
<h2 id="legal-toc-title">
<span class="sr-only">On this page</span>
<span class="ins" aria-hidden="true">on this page</span>
</h2>
<ol>
<li>
<a href="#agreement">Agreement</a>
</li>
<li>
<a href="#eligibility">Eligibility and your account</a>
</li>
<li>
<a href="#debates">Debates, recording and replay</a>
</li>
<li>
<a href="#content">Your content and our licence</a>
</li>
<li>
<a href="#conduct">Conduct</a>
</li>
<li>
<a href="#coins">Yap Coins</a>
</li>
<li>
<a href="#service">Our service</a>
</li>
<li>
<a href="#ending">Suspension and ending your account</a>
</li>
<li>
<a href="#liability">Liability</a>
</li>
<li>
<a href="#changes">Changes to these terms</a>
</li>
<li>
<a href="#law">Governing law</a>
</li>
<li>
<a href="#contact">Contact</a>
</li>
</ol>
</nav>
<article class="legal-body">
<section id="agreement" aria-labelledby="agreement-title">
<h2 id="agreement-title">Agreement</h2>
<p>By creating an account or using YAP Arena, you accept these terms and the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. If you don’t accept them, don’t use YAP Arena. New accounts confirm this when they claim their handle.</p>
<p>YAP Arena is operated by <mark class="legal-todo">[Legal name of the business]</mark>, <mark class="legal-todo">[Business address in Québec]</mark> (“YAP Arena”, “we”, “us”).</p>
</section>
<section id="eligibility" aria-labelledby="eligibility-title">
<h2 id="eligibility-title">Eligibility and your account</h2>
<ul>
<li>You must be <strong>18 or older</strong> and able to enter into a contract.</li>
<li>One person per account. Use your own email address or Google account and keep access to it secure: anyone who can read your email or use your Google account can sign in as you.</li>
<li>Your handle is permanent. Don’t choose a username or handle that impersonates someone, misleads people about who you are or breaks the conduct rules; we may change or remove one that does.</li>
<li>You are responsible for what happens through your account. Tell us at <mark class="legal-todo">[Contact email]</mark> if you think someone else is using it.</li>
</ul>
</section>
<section id="debates" aria-labelledby="debates-title">
<h2 id="debates-title">Debates, recording and replay</h2>
<div class="legal-note">
<p>Debates on YAP Arena are public. They are shown live, <strong>recorded on video and audio</strong> and <strong>published as replays</strong> that anyone can watch and share.</p>
</div>
<ul>
<li>Each turn is transcribed into captions and summarized in an <strong>AI outline</strong>. Both are automatic and can be wrong; they are not statements by YAP Arena or by the debater. YAP Arena does not declare winners.</li>
<li>To debate, you must agree to recording, public replay, transcription and the AI outline in the Debating card in your account settings.</li>
<li>Only show and say what you have the right to share. Don’t put other people on camera without their permission, and don’t play music, video or other material you don’t have the rights to.</li>
<li>We may pause, end, cancel or remove a debate, for example when it breaks these terms or a technical problem affects it.</li>
</ul>
</section>
<section id="content" aria-labelledby="content-title">
<h2 id="content-title">Your content and our licence</h2>
<p>You keep ownership of what you create on YAP Arena: your debate video and audio, what you say and write, your chat messages and your profile (“your content”).</p>
<p>You grant <mark class="legal-todo">[Legal name of the business]</mark> a non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free licence to host, store, record, reproduce, transcribe, caption, summarize (including with AI), adapt for format and length, publish, display, stream and distribute your content on YAP Arena and in links and previews of it, and to have our service providers do so for us. <mark class="legal-todo">[Founder: say whether YAP Arena may also use debate clips to promote itself elsewhere]</mark>
</p>
<p>The licence lasts as long as we keep your content under the Privacy Policy, and ends when it is deleted, except for copies in backups until they expire and copies others made while it was public. To the extent the law allows, you agree not to assert moral rights against changes needed only to format, caption or summarize your content.</p>
<p>You confirm that you have the rights needed to grant this licence. Other people’s debates and content belong to them: you may watch and share links to them, but don’t copy, re-publish or sell them beyond what the law allows.</p>
</section>
<section id="conduct" aria-labelledby="conduct-title">
<h2 id="conduct-title">Conduct</h2>
<p>Argue the idea, not the person. On YAP Arena, including debates, chat, profiles and usernames, you must not:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<strong>Harass</strong>, bully or threaten anyone, or encourage violence or self-harm.</li>
<li>Post <strong>hate</strong>: attacks on people for their race, ethnicity, national origin, religion, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, age or other protected characteristic.</li>
<li>Share <strong>private information</strong> about someone, such as their address, phone number or documents, or images of them without their consent.</li>
<li>Post <strong>spam</strong>, scams or misleading links, or impersonate a person or organization.</li>
<li>Show sexual content or nudity, or anything illegal.</li>
<li>
<strong>Manipulate</strong> YAP Arena: use bots or several accounts, coordinate to distort Yap Coins results, or try to take a position in your own debate.</li>
<li>Interfere with the service: attack, overload or probe it, get around limits or bans, or collect other people’s information by automated means.</li>
</ul>
<p>Anyone can report a chat message or a debate. Moderators may remove chat, pause a debate’s chat, restrict your community access for 7 days, or suspend or close your account. If a decision affects your chat or account, you can appeal once within 30 days from <a href="/account/moderation">your reports and appeals</a>; a different moderator decides.</p>
</section>
<section id="coins" aria-labelledby="coins-title">
<h2 id="coins-title">Yap Coins</h2>
<div class="legal-note">
<p>
<strong>Yap Coins are play money.</strong> They have no cash value and are not money, property, a currency or an investment.</p>
</div>
<ul>
<li>Every account receives a welcome grant of Yap Coins. You use them to answer each turn of a debate in a play-money game.</li>
<li>Yap Coins <strong>can’t be bought, sold, withdrawn, transferred to another account or exchanged</strong> for money, prizes or anything else of value. YAP Arena has no real-money features.</li>
<li>We may change the game’s rules, correct balances affected by errors, and adjust or remove Yap Coins obtained by breaking these terms. Closing an account ends its Yap Coins without compensation.</li>
<li>If YAP Arena ever offers anything of real value, it will come with separate terms that you accept first.</li>
</ul>
</section>
<section id="service" aria-labelledby="service-title">
<h2 id="service-title">Our service</h2>
<p>YAP Arena is new and changes often. We may add, change or remove features, and the service may be interrupted for maintenance or because of problems with our providers. We provide YAP Arena “as is” and don’t promise that it will always be available or free of errors.</p>
<p>What debaters and other users say is their own opinion. YAP Arena doesn’t endorse it, and it isn’t professional advice.</p>
</section>
<section id="ending" aria-labelledby="ending-title">
<h2 id="ending-title">Suspension and ending your account</h2>
<p>You can stop using YAP Arena at any time and ask us to delete your account at <mark class="legal-todo">[Contact email]</mark> (see the <a href="/privacy#rights">Privacy Policy</a>).</p>
<p>We may remove content, or suspend or close an account, if it breaks these terms, if the law requires it, or to protect people or YAP Arena. We tell you why unless the law or someone’s safety prevents it. When an account ends, its Yap Coins end, and its debates remain public under the Privacy Policy’s periods unless we remove them.</p>
</section>
<section id="liability" aria-labelledby="liability-title">
<h2 id="liability-title">Liability</h2>
<p>To the extent the law allows, <mark class="legal-todo">[Legal name of the business]</mark> is not liable for indirect or consequential losses, or for what other users say or do. Nothing in these terms limits rights you have as a consumer under the laws of Québec or Canada that can’t be waived, or our liability for our own intentional or gross fault.</p>
</section>
<section id="changes" aria-labelledby="changes-title">
<h2 id="changes-title">Changes to these terms</h2>
<p>We may update these terms. We post the new version here with its date and version. If a change is significant, we tell you in YAP Arena before it applies and ask you to accept the new version to keep using your account.</p>
</section>
<section id="law" aria-labelledby="law-title">
<h2 id="law-title">Governing law</h2>
<p>These terms are governed by the laws of Québec and the federal laws of Canada that apply there. Disputes go to the courts of the judicial district of <mark class="legal-todo">[Judicial district]</mark>, Québec, without limiting a consumer’s right to bring a claim where they live.</p>
</section>
<section id="contact" aria-labelledby="contact-title">
<h2 id="contact-title">Contact</h2>
<p>Questions about these terms go to <mark class="legal-todo">[Contact email]</mark>, or by mail to <mark class="legal-todo">[Legal name of the business]</mark>, <mark class="legal-todo">[Business address in Québec]</mark>.</p>
</section>
<a class="legal-top" href="#main">Back to top <span aria-hidden="true">↑</span>
</a>
</article>
</div>
</div>
</main>
